class Solution {
public:
    int rob(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();

        if (n == 1) {
            return nums[0];
        }

        vector<int> dp(n, 0);

        dp[0] = nums[0];
        dp[1] = max(nums[0], nums[1]);

        for (int i = 2; i < n; i++) {
            dp[i] = max(dp[i - 1], nums[i] + dp[i - 2]);
        }

        return dp[n - 1];        
    }
};
Explanation:
n = nums.size() stores the total number of houses.
If there is only one house, return its money (nums[0]).
Create a DP array dp of size n.
dp[i] stores the maximum money that can be robbed from houses 0 to i.
Initialize dp[0] = nums[0] because only the first house is available.
Initialize dp[1] = max(nums[0], nums[1]) since you can rob only one of the first two houses.
From i = 2 to n-1, consider each remaining house.
If you skip the current house, the money is dp[i-1].
If you rob the current house, the money is nums[i] + dp[i-2].
Store the maximum of these two choices in dp[i] and return dp[n-1] as the final answer.
